# interplay_lifetime_private_across_fifos: A private buffer filled on the worker FIFO (child 2) by an exec that lists it with invalidateGuest (2), then read on the root FIFO by execs gated on the worker's stamp. In-process the buffer is one host copy shared by every FIFO: read with flags 0 it shows the fill; read with invalidateHost (1), it is paged from its guest pages, which never saw the fill (invalidateHost makes the guest's copy the valid one, and nothing synchronized it), so the fill is gone for good, and a later read with flags 0 shows the guest's bytes. In the service the buffer is the guest pages, and every read shows the fill.
